From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:26:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 033/342] libroot/arm64: fix __swap_float and __swap_double

The fmov operands were reversed: AArch64's fmov takes the destination
first, so "fmov s0, w0" copied the integer register into the float
argument instead of the other way around. Both functions returned
whatever was in w0/x0, so every B_SWAP_FLOAT, B_HOST_TO_BENDIAN_FLOAT
and their double variants gave garbage on arm64.

Found through the JPEG translator: it writes its TranslatorBitmap header
bounds with B_HOST_TO_BENDIAN_FLOAT, so BBitmapStream got a bitmap one
row high and the translator wrote the image past it into app_server's
shared memory until it faulted (ShowImage, BTranslationUtils::GetBitmap).

Tested on the ODROID-C2: float and double swaps of several values match
a byte-wise swap and swap back; JPEGs up to 1920x1080 open in ShowImage
and another image viewer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/libroot/os/arch/arm64/byteorder.S | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/system/libroot/os/arch/arm64/byteorder.S b/src/system/libroot/os/arch/arm64/byteorder.S
index dc5ad70a94..77d0aa13c6 100644
--- a/src/system/libroot/os/arch/arm64/byteorder.S
+++ b/src/system/libroot/os/arch/arm64/byteorder.S
@@ -10,17 +10,17 @@
 
 /* float __swap_float(float value) */
 FUNCTION(__swap_float):
-		fmov s0, w0	// Bitcopy float to general register
+		fmov w0, s0	// Bitcopy float to general register
 		rev w0, w0	// GCC8.3 does this for __builtin_bswap32
-		fmov w0, s0	// and back
+		fmov s0, w0	// and back
 		ret
 FUNCTION_END(__swap_float)
 
 
 /* double __swap_double(double value) */
 FUNCTION(__swap_double):
-		fmov d0, x0	// Bitcopy double to general register
+		fmov x0, d0	// Bitcopy double to general register
 		rev x0, x0	// GCC8.3 does this for __builtin_bswap64
-		fmov x0, d0	// and back
+		fmov d0, x0	// and back
 		ret
 FUNCTION_END(__swap_double)
